t, born in Genoa, who became court architect in Vienna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-martin-honigberger"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-martin-honigberger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Martin Honigberger</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Martin Honigberger was a physician from Transylvania who served at the court of Ranjit Singh in Lahore.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-matthias-von-der-schulenburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-matthias-von-der-schulenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Matthias von der Schulenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Matthias von der Schulenburg was a German soldier who served Saxony and other powers before becoming field marshal of the Republic of Venice in 1715.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-michael-fischer"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-michael-fischer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Michael Fischer</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Michael Fischer was a Bavarian architect, one of the leading builders of the south German Baroque and Rococo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-of-manderscheid-blankenheim"><span class="enc-name">Johann of Manderscheid-Blankenheim</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann of Manderscheid-Blankenheim (1538–1592) was Bishop of Strasbourg from 1569.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-reinhard-iii-of-hanau"><span class="enc-name">Johann Reinhard III of Hanau</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Rein