" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Strauss II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Strauss II was an Austrian composer of light music and a violinist, born near Vienna, the son of the composer Johann Strauss I, who wrote over 500 waltzes…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly, was a Walloon general who commanded the army of the Catholic League in the Thirty Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-von-munchhausen"><span class="enc-name">Johann von Münchhausen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann von Münchhausen was a Livonian churchman of a Lower Saxon noble family who held the bishoprics of Ösel-Wiek and Courland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-weikhard-von-valvasor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-weikhard-von-valvasor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Weikhard von Valvasor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Weikhard von Valvasor was a Carniolan nobleman and polymath, born in Ljubljana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-wilhelm-ludwig-gleim"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-wilhelm-ludwig-gleim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Johann Wilhelm Ludwig Gleim</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Johann Wilhelm Ludwig Gleim was a German poet of the Anacreontic school who served from 1747